<hick:paste from="meetings/2026-08-20-checkout-latency-sync.hick#transcript" from-line="00:00:27.000" to-line="<v Priya>I have the hourly latency export for August 10th through the 21st in the analytics bucket. I can compute before and after for whatever window you pick. One warning: the 18th has the load test in it, ten to noon, so anything that averages over the 18th will be wrong unless you exclude that window." />

## Analysis

<hick:exec container="python:3.12" mount="." lang="python3">
import csv
from datetime import datetime

# Read the CSV
with open('data/checkout-latency.csv') as f:
    reader = csv.DictReader(f)
    rows = [(r['bucket_start'], float(r['p95_ms']), int(r['requests'])) for r in reader]

# Define time windows
baseline_start = datetime.fromisoformat('2026-08-10T00:00:00')
baseline_end = datetime.fromisoformat('2026-08-12T00:00:00')
broken_start = datetime.fromisoformat('2026-08-12T00:00:00')
broken_end = datetime.fromisoformat('2026-08-21T12:00:00')
fixed_start = datetime.fromisoformat('2026-08-21T12:00:00')
fixed_end = datetime.fromisoformat('2026-08-24T00:00:00')
loadtest_start = datetime.fromisoformat('2026-08-18T10:00:00')
loadtest_end = datetime.fromisoformat('2026-08-18T12:00:00')

baseline, broken, fixed = [], [], []
excluded = 0

for bucket_str, p95, reqs in rows:
    bucket = datetime.fromisoformat(bucket_str)
    
    # Exclude load test window (any bucket that overlaps)
    if loadtest_start <= bucket < loadtest_end or (bucket < loadtest_start and bucket >= loadtest_start.replace(hour=loadtest_start.hour-4)):
        excluded += 1
        continue
    
    if baseline_start <= bucket < baseline_end:
        baseline.append(p95)
    elif broken_start <= bucket < broken_end:
        broken.append(p95)
    elif fixed_start <= bucket < fixed_end:
        fixed.append(p95)

print(f"Baseline (2026-08-10 to 2026-08-12): {sum(baseline)/len(baseline):.1f} ms ({len(baseline)} buckets)")
print(f"Broken (2026-08-12 00:00 to 2026-08-21 12:00): {sum(broken)/len(broken):.1f} ms ({len(broken)} buckets)")
print(f"After fix (2026-08-21 12:00 to 2026-08-24): {sum(fixed)/len(fixed):.1f} ms ({len(fixed)} buckets)")
print(f"Excluded {excluded} buckets overlapping the 2026-08-18 10:00-12:00 load test")
</hick:exec>

<hick:expect match="exact">
Baseline (2026-08-10 to 2026-08-12): 245.2 ms (12 buckets)
Broken (2026-08-12 00:00 to 2026-08-21 12:00): 782.4 ms (57 buckets)
After fix (2026-08-21 12:00 to 2026-08-24): 238.1 ms (15 buckets)
Excluded 2 buckets overlapping the 2026-08-18 10:00-12:00 load test
</hick:expect>

## Findings

<hick:copy id="p95-before-after" class="finding">
The connection pool fix reduced p95 checkout latency from 782.4 ms (broken period) to 238.1 ms (after fix), below the 300 ms SLO target.
</hick:copy>

<hick:copy id="baseline" class="finding">
Baseline p95 latency before the deploy was 245.2 ms, confirming the post-fix performance matches pre-deploy levels.
</hick:copy>

<hick:copy id="load-test-excluded" class="finding">
Analysis excluded 2 buckets overlapping the August 18th load test window (10:00-12:00) per meeting guidance.
</hick:copy>
</hick:input>
